# What must never enter the image.
#
# The first block is a licence boundary, not an optimisation. Video-MME's terms forbid
# redistributing the media (data/corpus/PROVENANCE.md), and the corpus is pointers, not
# copies. An image layer is a copy, and a pushed image is redistribution. `samples/` and
# `runs/` are volumes at run time (see compose.yaml) precisely so the media reaches the
# container without ever being baked into it.
samples/
runs/
chroma/
*.mp4
*.wav
*.mkv
*.webm
*.m4a

# Secrets live in ~/.config/ and reach the container as environment variables (CLAUDE.md).
# src/env.py gives the process environment highest precedence, so nothing needs .env to be
# present. Baking one in would ship a credential inside a layer that `docker history` reads.
.env

# Build artefacts of the host. .venv/ especially: it holds platform-specific wheels built
# for the host OS, and copying a Windows venv into a Linux image produces an environment
# that imports nothing.
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Generated, and committing it would give a frontend two contracts to disagree about
# (see the `openapi` target in the Makefile).
openapi.json
